    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273-a4">

                <pb facs="0504" n="494" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg494"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 4 in No. 10.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Lord Lyons to Major General Doyle.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 4, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I had on the 26th ultimo the honor to
                    receive your excellency’s despatch of the 23d ultimo, enclosing a copy of a
                    despatch which you had addressed on <pb facs="0505" n="495" xml:id="pg495"/> the
                    same day to the Duke of Newcastle with regard to the affair of the Chesapeake. I
                    beg your excellency to accept my best thanks for the full information which you
                    have been so good as to send me respecting this affair.</p>
                <p>The Secretary of State of the United States has repeatedly promised me that the
                    assurance given in his note of the 18th ultimo shall be acted up to.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
